The only skills I think any programmer "needs" are:

1) a willingness to accept the truth that the machine is a predictable 
creature that will _always_ do _precisely_ what you tell it; any problems 
occur because you didn't realize or understand what it was being told.

2) a capacity to hold large abstract concepts and structures in your 
head, and the ability to examine those concepts/structures from multiple
angles.

I spend far more time thinking about what I'm going to write, both at my
job and with Spork, than I do actually typing lines of code.  It saves
having to come back and retype them later.

